{
    "m_SGVersion": 0,
    "m_Type": "UnityEditor.ShaderGraph.StickyNoteData",
    "m_ObjectId": "b118c35704404a548335fd6473b80ff0",
    "m_Title": "Solve Phases",
    "m_Content": "This function solves the phases for fluid flow. Because we are advecting the position we are sampling the noise, continuously pushing the same field would cause massive distortion in a very short time. Instead we use two different phases offset by 0.5 and blend between them. When one phase is fully visible, the other phase is reset so the flow vectors start back at 0 and scale up until the next phase swap. We also generated floored values for time to use in a hash function which randomly offsets the noise to prevent it from looking like the exact same 2 patterns are repeating in each phase.",
